<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Blunt. Pure stat mod, untagged (no exclusionTags — nothing to gate; stacks freely with any
       Head/SwingProfile pick). Flanges (or a studded/ridged head) concentrate the blow's force into a
       narrow ridge that cracks plate rather than punching through it — a distinct mechanism from
       UMW_ArmorSpike's Stab-tool piercing, so it floors deliberately lower: 0.45 vs ArmorSpike's 0.6
       (both in Normal-quality units on the same ladder as UMW_Monomolecular's 0.9). No damage change,
       no extra hit — the head shape alone raises the Blunt tool's floor.
       WHY QUALITY-SCALED (2026-11). The floor is MeleeToolModExtension's QUALITY floor, multiplied at
       swing time by the weapon's MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier quality factor, the way vanilla scales
       an explicit tool AP. The 1.x FLAT 0.45 assumed uniques span the quality range; they never roll
       below Masterwork (QualityGenerator.Super), and a default tool's AP is its damage x0.015, so a
       Masterwork steel warhammer head (0.43) already brushed the floor and uranium or jade heads
       (x1.5 blunt damage) cleared it outright: the trait was dead or near-dead on half its rolls.
       Scaled, a Masterwork steel mace head goes 0.34 to 0.65 and a warhammer 0.43 to 0.65, past every
       vanilla blunt rating (flak vest 0.36, recon 0.40, marine 0.45, cataphract 0.50). It stays dead
       on uranium and jade warhammers (own 0.65 to 0.74), accepted: those heads already out-pierce
       every vanilla blunt rating, and the cases are rare. Modded armor with higher blunt ratings
       makes the floor matter there again rather than breaking anything.
       Also matches Demolish (the breach axe, the only Demolish tool in the game) and
       VFEP_GravityHammerAttack (MayRequire VFE Pirates; VFEP's warcasket gravity hammer, whose only
       other tool is a Poke handle), so on those weapons the mod lands on the head the description
       talks about rather than on the handle or nothing. Both are BluntBase damages, so they sit in
       alsoMatches: the info-card line names only "blunt", and on every other weapon the entry is
       equivalent to Blunt alone.
       Priced at parity with Odyssey's ranged PiercingRounds (+40).
       Under Combat Extended the floor is restated in CE units, 8 MPa at Normal
       (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/WeaponTraits_CE.xml). -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_Flanged</defName>
    <label>flanged</label>
    <description>The head is ridged with flanges that concentrate the force of a blow into a narrow edge, cracking armor plate rather than denting it.</description>
    <commonality>1</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Blunt</weaponCategory>
    <statOffsets>
      <MarketValue>40</MarketValue> <!-- cf. PiercingRounds -->
    </statOffsets>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>flanged</li>
      <li>riving</li>
      <li>armor-cracking</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension">
        <mods>
          <li>
            <capacities>
              <li>Blunt</li>
            </capacities>
            <alsoMatches> <!-- blunt-damage heads, unnamed in the info card; see header -->
              <li>Demolish</li> <!-- breach axe -->
              <li MayRequire="OskarPotocki.VFE.Pirates">VFEP_GravityHammerAttack</li> <!-- VFEP gravity hammer -->
            </alsoMatches>
            <armorPenetrationQualityFloor>0.45</armorPenetrationQualityFloor> <!-- Normal-quality units; see header -->
          </li>
        </mods>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
